shocking claims that one of the  country's largest christian  denominations suppressed allegations of  sexual abuse for years a scathing new  report commissioned by the southern  baptist convention describes decades of  cover-ups within its clergy and  membership and leadership  the sbc is a network of roughly 47 000  independently run baptist churches with  more than 14 million members nationwide  nikki bautista is following this story  for us nikki this was a  self-commissioned report good morning  indeed tony good morning the report  alleges that claims of abuse were  catalogued internally for more than a  decade with little to no follow-up or  discipline for alleged perpetrators even  as sbc leadership was made aware of  accusations facing clergy the report  says its main concern was quote avoiding  any potential liability  the independent investigation  commissioned by the southern baptist  convention concluded that members of the  group's executive committee responded  with resistance stonewalling and even  outright hostility to almost two decades  of sexual abuse allegations against  clergy according to the report they kept  a secret running list of accused baptist  ministers to avoid being sued even as  the committee publicly claimed it didn't  have the authority to create such a list  more than 400 people on it were believed  to be affiliated with the sbc at some  point but the report quotes a may 9 2019  internal email where the sbc's then  general counsel called the focus on  sexual abuse  a satanic scheme to completely distract  us from evangelism every day is a  struggle  since i've come forward publicly hannah  kate williams filed a lawsuit against  the sbc on friday alleging that she was  physically abused by her own father a  pastor for years she says it began when  she was as young as four years old and  turned into sexual abuse on her eighth  birthday but when she sought help from  the sbc leadership she says nothing ever  happened when i was kicked down i was  called a liar i was called mentally  deranged incompetent  an enemy of god the report says the sbc  used its system of granting churches  autonomy to deflect accountability for  local offenders but allegations of abuse  go up to the very top including a sexual  assault claim against former sbc  president johnny hunt which he denied in  a facebook post sunday night what as a  survivor would you like to see change i  would like to see  leaders taking the recommendations of  outside experts not as attacks on their  beliefs  but as  tools to protect those in their care  in a statement the sbc's executive  committee said it was reviewing the  report and is quote committed to doing  all we can to prevent future instances  of sexual abuse in churches we also  reached out to hannah kate williams  father for comments but have not heard  back in the past few months i've spoken  with about a dozen other women and men  who claim they were sexually abused by  southern baptist convention leaders at  the time of the alleged abuse their ages  ranged from 9 to 14. those survivors are  all past their statutes of limitations  which means they can't file a lawsuit in  their respective states each of them  told me they hope this independent  report will lead to accountability and  this really reminds me of the catholic  church abuse survivors i've spoken with  in the past and each of these survivors  have said we just want to be believed  and i think this report will finally be  a step in the right direction that's an  awful story you know it's bad when  you're suing your own father you just  don't expect to hear sexual abuse and  church in the same sentence but  unfortunately we've heard this story  before she's incredibly brave yeah i  think so too thank you nikki
 

